# MCP Development

**Alpha** — prefer package `docs/index.md` over the README. APIs may still move. There is no Ignis `search-docs` tool for MCP.

## Documentation

Read package `docs/index.md` for detailed CakePHP MCP patterns.

For MCP UI apps (interactive HTML resources), read `references/app.md` — it covers the full architecture, host theming CSS variables, tool-to-UI linking patterns, library scripts (Tailwind, Alpine via `Library`), and real-world examples.

## Basic Usage

Register MCP servers in `config/mcp.php` under `Mcp.Servers` (HTTP) and `Mcp.local` (STDIO), or via `Registrar::web()` / `local()` per docs.

```bash
composer require crustum/mcp
{{ assist.cakeCommand('plugin load Crustum/Mcp') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('manifest install --plugin Crustum/Mcp') }}
```

### Creating MCP Primitives

```bash
{{ assist.cakeCommand('bake mcp_tool ToolName') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('bake mcp_resource ResourceName') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('bake mcp_prompt PromptName') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('bake mcp_server ServerName') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('bake mcp_app_resource DashboardApp') }}
```

After creating primitives, register them in your server's `$tools`, `$resources`, or `$prompts` properties. Host namespaces (default): `App\Mcp\Servers|Tools|Prompts|Resources`.

### Tools

@ignissnippet("MCP Tool Example", "php")
use Crustum\Mcp\Request;
use Crustum\Mcp\Response;
use Crustum\Mcp\Server\Tool;
use Illuminate\Contracts\JsonSchema\JsonSchema;

class MyTool extends Tool
{
    protected string $description = 'Describe what this tool does';

    public function schema(JsonSchema $schema): array
    {
        return [
            'name' => $schema->string()->description('The name parameter')->required(),
        ];
    }

    public function handle(Request $request): Response
    {
        $request->validate(['name' => 'required|string']);

        return Response::text('Hello, '.$request->get('name'));
    }
}
@endignissnippet

`JsonSchema` comes from the `illuminate/json-schema` dependency (tool input/output schema builder).

### Registering Primitives in a Server

@ignissnippet("Register Primitives in MCP Server", "php")
use Crustum\Mcp\Server;

class AppServer extends Server
{
    protected array $tools = [
        \App\Mcp\Tools\MyTool::class,
    ];

    protected array $resources = [
        \App\Mcp\Resources\MyResource::class,
    ];

    protected array $prompts = [
        \App\Mcp\Prompts\MyPrompt::class,
    ];
}
@endignissnippet

Expose the server via `Mcp.Servers` / `Mcp.local` in `config/mcp.php` (or `Registrar::web()` / `local()`).

