## Verification

1. Check `config/mcp.php` → `Mcp.Servers` / `Mcp.local` for proper registration
2. Test tool via MCP client / `{{ assist.cakeCommand('mcp inspector') }}`

## Common Pitfalls

- Running `{{ assist.cakeCommand('mcp start …') }}` in a normal terminal — it hangs waiting for STDIO JSON-RPC (MCP clients own the process)
- Using HTTPS locally with Node-based MCP clients / inspector — prefer HTTP in local dev
- Guessing APIs from memory — prefer package `docs/index.md` (no Ignis MCP `search-docs` tool)
- Not registering web servers in `config/mcp.php` → `Mcp.Servers` (or `Registrar::web`)
- Duplicating registration by hand in routes/bootstrap when `Mcp.Servers` / `Mcp.local` already cover it — the registrar loads those entries automatically
- OAuth for native desktop clients (`cursor://`, `vscode://`, …) — add allowed schemes under `Mcp.custom_schemes` in `config/mcp.php`
- Baking primitives but leaving them off the server `$tools` / `$resources` / `$prompts` arrays
- Tools that take arguments without a matching `schema()`
